1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,003
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:06,006
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:44,043
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:46,879
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,966
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:53,553
[mouse clicking]

7
00:00:57,099 --> 00:00:59,433
Jin Isoo is late today.
We had a drink yesterday.

8
00:00:59,434 --> 00:01:00,519
Did you?

9
00:01:00,936 --> 00:01:02,604
[exhales] He must've lost again.

10
00:01:02,854 --> 00:01:04,231
EPISODE 11

11
00:01:07,526 --> 00:01:08,819
- Oh.
- [Changun] Uh...

12
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:10,571
Detective Joo.

13
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:13,864
We got a report from Jin Isoo's house.

14
00:01:13,865 --> 00:01:14,991
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

15
00:01:14,992 --> 00:01:16,368
You should go check it out.

16
00:01:21,123 --> 00:01:22,708
[tires screeching]

17
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:32,801
This way, please.

18
00:01:34,761 --> 00:01:36,930
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

19
00:02:02,581 --> 00:02:04,040
[Younghwan laughing] <i>Huh?</i>

20
00:02:04,041 --> 00:02:06,335
<i>My friend, Jin Isoo.</i> [laughs]

21
00:02:07,627 --> 00:02:08,795
[Isoo] <i>Younghwan, you, again!</i>

22
00:02:09,504 --> 00:02:10,588
You want to try, too?

23
00:02:10,589 --> 00:02:12,590
No! Please... Don't!

24
00:02:12,591 --> 00:02:15,552
I told you I'd never see you
if you did it again.

25
00:02:21,892 --> 00:02:24,352
<i>You should undergo
a proper investigation and quit drugs.</i>

26
00:02:24,353 --> 00:02:27,773
All my life,
I've never thought of you as a friend.

27
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:30,651
[♪ tense, pulsating music playing]

28
00:02:43,246 --> 00:02:44,247
Jin Isoo.

29
00:02:49,461 --> 00:02:50,879
[♪ music swells]

30
00:03:02,391 --> 00:03:03,684
[♪ music resumes tempo]

31
00:03:12,776 --> 00:03:14,402
That's Kim Younghwan.

32
00:03:14,403 --> 00:03:16,029
[♪ music increases in tempo]

33
00:03:18,198 --> 00:03:19,324
What happened?

34
00:03:35,048 --> 00:03:36,341
[♪ music swells]

35
00:03:40,554 --> 00:03:41,846
[♪ music fades]

36
00:03:41,847 --> 00:03:43,223
[♪ ominous music playing]

37
00:03:44,433 --> 00:03:45,767
[camera shutter clicking]

38
00:03:54,943 --> 00:03:56,194
[♪ music fades]

39
00:03:58,321 --> 00:04:00,615
Do you two know who the victim is?

40
00:04:01,366 --> 00:04:03,160
He's Isoo's friend from middle school.

41
00:04:03,869 --> 00:04:06,328
He was the CEO
of the production company Isoo owns.

42
00:04:06,329 --> 00:04:08,247
Isoo personally arrested him for drugs.

43
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:10,959
I looked into it,
and he was released two months ago.

44
00:04:17,048 --> 00:04:18,216
What happened?

45
00:04:18,925 --> 00:04:21,261
What time did you get home
after we split up?

46
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:27,850
I think it was after 10:00 p.m.

47
00:04:27,851 --> 00:04:29,186
And then?

48
00:04:30,103 --> 00:04:31,687
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

49
00:04:31,688 --> 00:04:32,981
[sighs softly]

50
00:04:45,952 --> 00:04:47,120
[digital lock beeps]

51
00:04:48,747 --> 00:04:50,080
[Younghwan laughing]

52
00:04:50,081 --> 00:04:52,541
Look who's here!

53
00:04:52,542 --> 00:04:54,211
My friend, Jin Isoo!

54
00:04:57,088 --> 00:04:58,964
I've been waiting for you.

55
00:04:58,965 --> 00:05:01,008
What took you so long?

56
00:05:01,009 --> 00:05:02,177
How did you...

57
00:05:04,387 --> 00:05:06,096
[chuckles softly]

58
00:05:06,097 --> 00:05:07,473
I gave you a key before.

59
00:05:07,474 --> 00:05:09,434
[chuckles] Exactly.

60
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:12,979
To your best friend. Did you forget?

61
00:05:14,815 --> 00:05:16,733
Wait a minute, you bastard.

62
00:05:17,609 --> 00:05:21,487
Did you erase
my very existence from your memory?

63
00:05:21,488 --> 00:05:23,906
Yes, I did.

64
00:05:23,907 --> 00:05:25,158
So just leave.

65
00:05:26,910 --> 00:05:29,120
Come on, don't be like that. It hurts.

66
00:05:29,913 --> 00:05:32,040
Just come sit down.

67
00:05:32,666 --> 00:05:33,667
Uh...

68
00:05:36,753 --> 00:05:39,922
[sighs] You did a fine job making this.

69
00:05:39,923 --> 00:05:41,799
It's classy.

70
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:43,510
Tasty, too. [chuckles]

71
00:05:47,222 --> 00:05:48,722
What are you playing at?

72
00:05:48,723 --> 00:05:51,225
Your friend came to visit, you asshole.

73
00:05:51,226 --> 00:05:52,978
Let's have a drink like old times.

74
00:05:55,605 --> 00:05:57,107
Drink up.

75
00:05:58,692 --> 00:05:59,860
[sighs softly]

76
00:06:02,279 --> 00:06:03,363
[exhales sharply]

77
00:06:04,447 --> 00:06:05,740
Didn't you miss me?

78
00:06:08,034 --> 00:06:09,244
Finish your drink and go.

79
00:06:09,995 --> 00:06:11,162
As for me,

80
00:06:13,039 --> 00:06:15,375
I thought about you a lot.

81
00:06:17,794 --> 00:06:20,671
ONE WEEK EARLIER

82
00:06:20,672 --> 00:06:21,882
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

83
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:29,681
Hey.

84
00:06:32,601 --> 00:06:34,810
Were you the one
who came in here last week?

85
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:36,437
[chuckling]

86
00:06:36,438 --> 00:06:38,188
Bingo!

87
00:06:38,189 --> 00:06:39,524
[laughs smugly]

88
00:06:41,276 --> 00:06:43,987
I came because I missed you so much.

89
00:06:46,448 --> 00:06:51,661
You didn't even visit me in prison,
or bother to come the day I got out.

90
00:06:54,914 --> 00:06:57,416
If you were the one to put me away,

91
00:06:57,417 --> 00:06:59,836
the least you could've done
was check in on me.

92
00:07:00,712 --> 00:07:03,673
After all those years I spent
as your damn sidekick.

93
00:07:05,592 --> 00:07:08,511
No matter how hard I try,
I can't get over it.

94
00:07:09,179 --> 00:07:10,430
But what do you know?

95
00:07:12,182 --> 00:07:13,892
[vocalizing victory fanfare]

96
00:07:15,644 --> 00:07:17,186
[laughs smugly]

97
00:07:17,187 --> 00:07:19,481
I have a key to your house.

98
00:07:21,191 --> 00:07:23,151
[breathes deeply]

99
00:07:24,027 --> 00:07:26,320
You knocked yourself out
with sleeping pills

100
00:07:26,321 --> 00:07:28,364
and couldn't remember a damn thing.

101
00:07:28,365 --> 00:07:29,449
[♪ music swells]

102
00:07:30,659 --> 00:07:31,951
[♪ ominous music playing]

103
00:07:38,917 --> 00:07:40,335
MR. JIN ISOO

104
00:07:55,225 --> 00:07:57,560
You're nothing, you piece of shit.

105
00:07:59,562 --> 00:08:01,356
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

106
00:08:18,873 --> 00:08:19,916
[blunt thud]

107
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:23,377
[clattering]

108
00:08:23,378 --> 00:08:25,170
- [exclaims]
- [glass shattering]

109
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:26,339
[exclaims]

110
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,216
[breathing heavily]

111
00:08:33,012 --> 00:08:34,139
[shatters]

112
00:08:34,472 --> 00:08:36,765
[laughing maniacally]

113
00:08:36,766 --> 00:08:38,016
[♪ music swells]

114
00:08:38,017 --> 00:08:40,061
[exclaims, continues laughing]

115
00:08:40,937 --> 00:08:43,355
I could have killed you.

116
00:08:43,356 --> 00:08:45,608
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

117
00:08:48,987 --> 00:08:51,488
I sent you to prison
to straighten you out,

118
00:08:51,489 --> 00:08:52,615
but you came back worse.

119
00:08:54,451 --> 00:08:55,534
Hey,

120
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:57,662
get up and leave while I'm being nice.

121
00:08:58,830 --> 00:08:59,831
What about you?

122
00:09:03,835 --> 00:09:06,336
What would happen

123
00:09:06,337 --> 00:09:09,340
if the great Jin Isoo ended up in prison?

124
00:09:10,216 --> 00:09:13,260
[scoffs] Now that would be
quite a sight, right?

125
00:09:13,261 --> 00:09:15,722
Cut the crap and get up.

126
00:09:18,808 --> 00:09:20,100
Do I have to drag you out?

127
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:21,227
[scoffs softly]

128
00:09:22,395 --> 00:09:23,772
Okay, fine.

129
00:09:25,273 --> 00:09:27,191
[in English] Okay. [grunts]

130
00:09:27,192 --> 00:09:28,193
My key.

131
00:09:29,235 --> 00:09:30,278
[in Korean] Right, your key.

132
00:09:34,365 --> 00:09:35,408
[scoffs]

133
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:37,035
[key card slaps on table]

134
00:09:42,415 --> 00:09:44,250
That hurts, you asshole.

135
00:09:47,170 --> 00:09:48,213
[sighs in exasperation]

136
00:09:51,758 --> 00:09:54,052
Let's shake hands one last time.

137
00:09:57,847 --> 00:09:59,682
I'm moving abroad.

138
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:03,352
I can't live here
after the way you humiliated me.

139
00:10:03,353 --> 00:10:04,395
[exhales softly]

140
00:10:08,817 --> 00:10:10,026
[♪ music turns ominous]

141
00:10:12,904 --> 00:10:14,404
[laughing maliciously]

142
00:10:14,405 --> 00:10:15,573
[♪ music increases in tempo]

143
00:10:16,366 --> 00:10:17,367
Jin Isoo.

144
00:10:18,868 --> 00:10:19,869
Enjoy the fall.

145
00:10:23,873 --> 00:10:25,624
You're finished.

146
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:26,918
[♪ music resumes tempo]

147
00:10:28,253 --> 00:10:29,629
[dull, distorted audio]

148
00:10:39,389 --> 00:10:40,973
[high-pitched tone droning]

149
00:10:40,974 --> 00:10:43,100
- [♪ music swells, fades]
- [muffled thuds]

150
00:10:43,101 --> 00:10:46,103
- [audio normalizes]
- [Younghwan laughing maliciously, echoes]

151
00:10:46,104 --> 00:10:47,479
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

152
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:48,564
[chair squeaks]

153
00:10:48,565 --> 00:10:49,773
[sighs in despair]

154
00:10:49,774 --> 00:10:51,109
That's all?

155
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:55,779
I don't remember anything after that.
I think I passed out.

156
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:57,365
[Kyungjin] How can you not remember?

157
00:10:58,032 --> 00:11:00,033
You're... [sighs softly]

158
00:11:00,034 --> 00:11:01,786
This is driving me crazy, too.

159
00:11:02,745 --> 00:11:04,414
How on earth did this happen?

160
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:06,790
[door bursts open]

161
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:08,292
[Taegyun] What the hell is going on?

162
00:11:08,293 --> 00:11:09,501
[♪ music fades]

163
00:11:09,502 --> 00:11:10,503
[exhales deeply]

164
00:11:14,132 --> 00:11:16,717
Joo Hyera. I told you, didn't I?

165
00:11:16,718 --> 00:11:18,553
I said he was going to cause trouble!

166
00:11:19,512 --> 00:11:20,555
[exclaims incredulously]

167
00:11:21,639 --> 00:11:22,724
You kept defending him.

168
00:11:23,558 --> 00:11:26,602
A police detective killed someone.
How are you going to fix this?

169
00:11:26,603 --> 00:11:29,146
- We still need to investigate.
- Investigate what?

170
00:11:29,147 --> 00:11:32,399
Jin Isoo and the victim were
the only ones inside the house!

171
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:34,277
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

172
00:11:35,486 --> 00:11:38,198
Hand over the case
to the Metropolitan Detective Unit.

173
00:11:38,990 --> 00:11:40,366
And you, come with me!

174
00:11:41,284 --> 00:11:42,285
[Taegyun scoffs softly]

175
00:11:45,205 --> 00:11:46,789
- [door slams]
- [sighs softly]

176
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:49,959
[Kyungjin sighs heavily]

177
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:52,294
Jin Isoo.

178
00:11:52,295 --> 00:11:54,923
You need to get it together
and remember anything you can.

179
00:11:57,091 --> 00:11:58,259
[sighs grimly]

180
00:12:00,553 --> 00:12:01,637
Where is Jin Isoo?

181
00:12:01,638 --> 00:12:02,972
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

182
00:12:06,476 --> 00:12:07,893
What are you going to do?

183
00:12:07,894 --> 00:12:10,771
We're arresting him without a warrant.
He has money and power.

184
00:12:10,772 --> 00:12:12,189
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE
KANG MUJIN

185
00:12:12,190 --> 00:12:13,608
No one's a bigger flight risk.

186
00:12:14,859 --> 00:12:16,318
Go and bring him out.

187
00:12:16,319 --> 00:12:17,862
- [detective 1] Yes, sir.
- [detective 2] Yes, sir.

188
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:21,907
[♪ music increases in tempo]

189
00:12:21,908 --> 00:12:22,909
[detective 1] Come with us.

190
00:12:23,618 --> 00:12:24,661
[Isoo grunts softly]

191
00:12:26,162 --> 00:12:27,163
[sighs softly]

192
00:12:35,213 --> 00:12:36,964
[Mujin] Mr. Jin Isoo,

193
00:12:36,965 --> 00:12:39,800
you are under arrest
for the murder of Kim Younghwan.

194
00:12:39,801 --> 00:12:43,178
You have the right to an attorney
and the right to remain silent.

195
00:12:43,179 --> 00:12:46,390
You won't be penalized
for remaining silent.

196
00:12:46,391 --> 00:12:48,600
You'll have a chance to explain yourself.

197
00:12:48,601 --> 00:12:50,269
[♪ music swells]

198
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:52,689
I'm sure you know from playing detective.

199
00:12:54,649 --> 00:12:55,650
Let's go.

200
00:12:57,318 --> 00:13:00,028
Please go out the back.
There are reporters outside.

201
00:13:00,029 --> 00:13:01,072
[♪ music fades]

202
00:13:06,536 --> 00:13:08,537
It really does pay to be a chaebol.

203
00:13:08,538 --> 00:13:11,373
How much will I get for that favor?
Maybe 100 million won?

204
00:13:11,374 --> 00:13:12,959
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

205
00:13:16,379 --> 00:13:17,630
He's not the killer.

206
00:13:18,256 --> 00:13:20,674
He would never kill anyone.

207
00:13:20,675 --> 00:13:21,800
[sighs softly]

208
00:13:21,801 --> 00:13:24,929
How much has he been slipping you
to make you say crap like that?

209
00:13:25,888 --> 00:13:28,307
You should worry about yourselves.

210
00:13:28,308 --> 00:13:30,059
Internal Affairs will be here soon.

211
00:13:31,561 --> 00:13:32,603
Let's go.

212
00:13:34,939 --> 00:13:36,190
[door opens]

213
00:13:36,858 --> 00:13:37,942
[scoffs softly]

214
00:13:38,401 --> 00:13:39,444
[door closes]

215
00:13:43,322 --> 00:13:45,240
[camera shutters clicking]

216
00:13:45,241 --> 00:13:47,534
[reporter 1] Is it true
that you murdered someone?

217
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:49,453
[reporter 2] Is it true
that the victim was a friend?

218
00:13:49,454 --> 00:13:52,080
- [reporter 3] Why did you kill him?
- [reporter 4] Mr. Jin Isoo!

219
00:13:52,081 --> 00:13:53,331
Do you admit to the murder?

220
00:13:53,332 --> 00:13:55,459
- [reporter 5] Was the murder premeditated?
- [reporter 6] Do you admit to it?

221
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:56,918
[reporters clamoring]

222
00:13:56,919 --> 00:13:58,337
[♪ tense, somber music playing]

223
00:14:05,178 --> 00:14:06,970
[clamoring continues]

224
00:14:06,971 --> 00:14:08,889
- [reporter 6] Mr. Jin Isoo!
- [siren blaring]

225
00:14:08,890 --> 00:14:09,891
[reporter 7] Mr. Jin Isoo!

226
00:14:11,017 --> 00:14:12,185
[clamor subsides]

227
00:14:13,269 --> 00:14:14,270
What do we do?

228
00:14:16,814 --> 00:14:17,981
[♪ music fades]

229
00:14:17,982 --> 00:14:19,734
[♪ pulsating ominous music playing]

230
00:14:41,756 --> 00:14:44,132
- [cell phone vibrating]
- [♪ music fades]

231
00:14:44,133 --> 00:14:46,802
JUNYOUNG

232
00:14:46,803 --> 00:14:48,888
- [line ringing, connects]
- [Dr. Yoon] <i>Junyoung.</i>

233
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:51,557
Did you see the body?

234
00:14:52,183 --> 00:14:54,352
[Dr. Yoon] Yes,
I'm looking at him right now.

235
00:14:56,229 --> 00:14:58,314
He was stabbed without hesitation.

236
00:14:59,315 --> 00:15:01,359
Did Detective Jin really do this?

237
00:15:02,527 --> 00:15:04,361
Absolutely not.

238
00:15:04,362 --> 00:15:05,571
It wasn't Isoo.

239
00:15:07,406 --> 00:15:08,491
[sighs softly]

240
00:15:08,991 --> 00:15:10,993
[♪ suspenseful, ticking music playing]

241
00:15:11,828 --> 00:15:13,371
[Mujin] How do you know Kim Younghwan?

242
00:15:16,415 --> 00:15:18,125
You're old friends

243
00:15:18,126 --> 00:15:20,044
and started a production company together?

244
00:15:21,170 --> 00:15:22,255
Yes.

245
00:15:22,713 --> 00:15:24,423
But you arrested him for doing drugs.

246
00:15:26,926 --> 00:15:28,051
[sighs wearily]

247
00:15:28,052 --> 00:15:31,764
He couldn't get off drugs,
so I turned him over to Narcotics.

248
00:15:33,015 --> 00:15:34,267
You're a good friend.

249
00:15:35,518 --> 00:15:37,145
But Kim Younghwan must've been mad.

250
00:15:37,854 --> 00:15:39,354
His friend had betrayed him.

251
00:15:39,355 --> 00:15:40,897
[♪ music increases in tempo]

252
00:15:40,898 --> 00:15:44,152
<i>Kim Younghwan entered your home
at 9:00 p.m. and waited for you.</i>

253
00:15:47,113 --> 00:15:48,446
[card reader beeps]

254
00:15:48,447 --> 00:15:49,991
You had a fight, didn't you?

255
00:15:51,075 --> 00:15:53,076
Things weren't exactly
pleasant between us.

256
00:15:53,077 --> 00:15:54,536
I told him to just leave.

257
00:15:54,537 --> 00:15:56,913
If you had a fight,
why did you do drugs together?

258
00:15:56,914 --> 00:15:58,039
[♪ music fades]

259
00:15:58,040 --> 00:15:59,083
Drugs?

260
00:16:01,586 --> 00:16:03,044
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

261
00:16:03,045 --> 00:16:04,796
[Mujin] This is the drug test
you just took.

262
00:16:04,797 --> 00:16:07,757
Judging by the levels,
you were completely out of it yesterday.

263
00:16:07,758 --> 00:16:08,801
NARCOTICS DETECTED

264
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:12,220
I don't do drugs.

265
00:16:12,221 --> 00:16:13,598
Then how do you explain this?

266
00:16:15,266 --> 00:16:16,309
[sighs in despair]

267
00:16:18,436 --> 00:16:20,020
Jin Isoo.

268
00:16:20,021 --> 00:16:21,147
Enjoy the fall.

269
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:23,566
You're finished.

270
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:26,193
[dull, distorted audio]

271
00:16:26,194 --> 00:16:27,485
[muffled thuds]

272
00:16:27,486 --> 00:16:29,905
A drug that can be absorbed
through skin contact.

273
00:16:29,906 --> 00:16:31,157
I think that's what got me.

274
00:16:31,824 --> 00:16:35,118
I don't remember anything
after shaking hands with Younghwan.

275
00:16:35,119 --> 00:16:36,494
[scoffs]

276
00:16:36,495 --> 00:16:38,288
Are you claiming diminished capacity?

277
00:16:38,289 --> 00:16:39,624
It's the truth.

278
00:16:40,249 --> 00:16:43,336
My team found a drug called "Ruby"
during one of our investigations.

279
00:16:46,255 --> 00:16:47,882
I think it was a similar drug.

280
00:16:49,342 --> 00:16:50,509
[sighs heavily]

281
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:52,802
[♪ music fades]

282
00:16:52,803 --> 00:16:56,014
We're both detectives here,
so let's be honest.

283
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:57,599
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

284
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:59,518
Imagine you're the detective in charge.

285
00:17:00,186 --> 00:17:02,896
Only the victim and the suspect
were present on site.

286
00:17:02,897 --> 00:17:04,857
The two of them are friends,

287
00:17:05,524 --> 00:17:08,110
but the suspect got the victim
convicted on drug charges.

288
00:17:09,612 --> 00:17:10,863
It's enough for a grudge.

289
00:17:11,614 --> 00:17:14,491
The victim was mad
and entered the suspect's home.

290
00:17:14,492 --> 00:17:16,410
The victim died,

291
00:17:17,286 --> 00:17:19,330
and the suspect was high on drugs.

292
00:17:20,998 --> 00:17:22,624
That's not all.

293
00:17:22,625 --> 00:17:25,085
The suspect is a chaebol
who does whatever he wants,

294
00:17:25,086 --> 00:17:28,047
and he carries the trauma
of having both his parents murdered.

295
00:17:30,174 --> 00:17:31,551
What do you think?

296
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:34,053
He looks guilty to you too, right?

297
00:17:36,514 --> 00:17:37,931
It really wasn't me.

298
00:17:37,932 --> 00:17:40,268
Then why did Kim Younghwan die?
Did he kill himself?

299
00:17:41,727 --> 00:17:43,186
You said someone reported it.

300
00:17:43,187 --> 00:17:45,063
Are you investigating them?

301
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:46,065
[scoffs]

302
00:17:46,941 --> 00:17:48,024
I am.

303
00:17:48,025 --> 00:17:49,193
Who is it?

304
00:17:49,777 --> 00:17:51,320
You can listen to it yourself.

305
00:17:54,615 --> 00:17:57,867
[Isoo, over recording]
<i>Hello? Please get the police here.</i>

306
00:17:57,868 --> 00:17:59,911
<i>I killed someone.</i>

307
00:17:59,912 --> 00:18:01,372
[dispatcher] <i>Sir, what is your name?</i>

308
00:18:02,498 --> 00:18:03,916
[Isoo] <i>Jin Isoo.</i>

309
00:18:04,709 --> 00:18:06,876
<i>I'm at my house.</i>

310
00:18:06,877 --> 00:18:07,920
[scoffs]

311
00:18:08,421 --> 00:18:09,422
What?

312
00:18:10,006 --> 00:18:11,464
Got nothing left to argue?

313
00:18:11,465 --> 00:18:12,925
[♪ music increases in tempo]

314
00:18:20,516 --> 00:18:22,726
- [Mr. Choi exhales sharply]
- [Mujin sighs]

315
00:18:22,727 --> 00:18:23,810
[♪ music resumes tempo]

316
00:18:23,811 --> 00:18:26,397
I'm done here, so feel free to talk.

317
00:18:32,695 --> 00:18:33,946
[door closes]

318
00:18:35,114 --> 00:18:36,282
[Mr. Choi sighs softly]

319
00:18:36,907 --> 00:18:37,991
[♪ music fades]

320
00:18:37,992 --> 00:18:40,285
[Changun] Don't get involved
and just stay put.

321
00:18:40,286 --> 00:18:42,830
And make sure Park and Choi
don't do anything stupid.

322
00:18:45,458 --> 00:18:47,959
Internal Affairs will be here.
If anything goes wrong,

323
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:49,545
all your careers are over.

324
00:18:50,755 --> 00:18:53,006
- Leave it with the Metropolitan Unit.
- I can't.

325
00:18:53,007 --> 00:18:54,591
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

326
00:18:54,592 --> 00:18:56,384
They already have a story worked out.

327
00:18:56,385 --> 00:18:58,471
They won't consider
any other possibilities.

328
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:04,644
Jin Isoo killing someone?

329
00:19:05,394 --> 00:19:06,645
I don't believe it.

330
00:19:06,646 --> 00:19:08,230
You never know with people.

331
00:19:08,898 --> 00:19:10,483
Jin Isoo could be the killer.

332
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:12,485
Even if that's true,

333
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:14,944
I need to see it for myself.

334
00:19:14,945 --> 00:19:16,112
Hey, Joo Hyera.

335
00:19:16,113 --> 00:19:17,114
Sir.

336
00:19:18,783 --> 00:19:21,827
If I were in this situation,
would you stand by and do nothing?

337
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:24,121
[sighs wearily]

338
00:19:28,793 --> 00:19:31,796
For now, there is a way
to prevent him from being detained.

339
00:19:32,338 --> 00:19:34,172
We can dispute this warrantless arrest.

340
00:19:34,173 --> 00:19:35,633
[Isoo] Please don't do that.

341
00:19:38,761 --> 00:19:39,970
I'm a police detective.

342
00:19:41,597 --> 00:19:43,973
I can't use a legal loophole
to run away from this.

343
00:19:43,974 --> 00:19:45,017
Isoo.

344
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:47,268
This isn't the time for that.

345
00:19:47,269 --> 00:19:48,270
[Isoo] Mr. Choi.

346
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:52,692
I didn't do it.

347
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:55,903
I need to catch...

348
00:19:57,238 --> 00:19:58,531
whoever did this.

349
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:06,121
[Mr. Choi sighs heavily]

350
00:20:06,122 --> 00:20:07,414
[♪ music fades]

351
00:20:07,415 --> 00:20:10,792
<i>Detective Jin Isoo of Gangha Police,
known for being a chaebol heir,</i>

352
00:20:10,793 --> 00:20:12,669
<i>has been arrested on a murder charge.</i>

353
00:20:12,670 --> 00:20:15,839
<i>Police reportedly made
a warrantless arrest</i>

354
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:18,383
<i>after the victim's body was found
inside his home.</i>

355
00:20:18,384 --> 00:20:20,760
<i>With public attention focused on this case</i>

356
00:20:20,761 --> 00:20:22,846
<i>involving the family
that owns Hansu Group,</i>

357
00:20:22,847 --> 00:20:26,016
<i>police are investigating the circumstances
surrounding the incident.</i>

358
00:20:27,017 --> 00:20:29,060
[news anchor] <i>Detective Jin Isoo,
the chaebol heir</i>

359
00:20:29,061 --> 00:20:30,478
<i>currently working as a detective,</i>

360
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:32,397
<i>was arrested on suspicion of murder.</i>

361
00:20:32,398 --> 00:20:33,732
<i>What exactly transpired?</i>

362
00:20:33,733 --> 00:20:37,068
[reporter] <i>Yes, a body was found
inside the home of Detective Jin Isoo.</i>

363
00:20:37,069 --> 00:20:39,738
<i>Detective Jin Isoo was
the only person inside the house,</i>

364
00:20:39,739 --> 00:20:43,491
<i>and an arrest warrant was issued after
multiple pieces of evidence were found.</i>

365
00:20:43,492 --> 00:20:46,453
<i>He is currently being questioned
by Seoul Metropolitan Police.</i>

366
00:20:46,454 --> 00:20:48,163
Isoo's gotten himself into trouble.

367
00:20:48,164 --> 00:20:49,540
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

368
00:20:58,090 --> 00:21:01,509
[Younghwan, laughing] <i>Look who's here!</i>

369
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:03,595
My friend, Jin Isoo!

370
00:21:03,596 --> 00:21:06,557
As for me, I thought about you a lot.

371
00:21:07,641 --> 00:21:10,101
What would happen

372
00:21:10,102 --> 00:21:13,313
if the great Jin Isoo ended up in prison?

373
00:21:13,314 --> 00:21:15,690
Let's shake hands one last time.

374
00:21:15,691 --> 00:21:17,109
[laughing maliciously]

375
00:21:18,486 --> 00:21:20,236
- [heavy thud]
- Jin Isoo.

376
00:21:20,237 --> 00:21:21,405
<i>Enjoy the fall.</i>

377
00:21:25,409 --> 00:21:26,577
[♪ music fades]

378
00:21:28,579 --> 00:21:30,915
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

379
00:21:36,462 --> 00:21:37,587
[door closes]

380
00:21:37,588 --> 00:21:39,632
Detective Joo, what do we do?

381
00:21:40,925 --> 00:21:42,383
[Junyoung] Let's investigate it ourselves.

382
00:21:42,384 --> 00:21:43,969
There's no way Isoo did this.

383
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:46,179
[Kyungjin] We need to do something.

384
00:21:46,180 --> 00:21:50,391
There's too much evidence against him.
If this goes to trial now, he's finished.

385
00:21:50,392 --> 00:21:52,685
[breathes deeply]
Getting worked up won't help.

386
00:21:52,686 --> 00:21:53,937
You two should stay put.

387
00:21:53,938 --> 00:21:55,439
Are you going to do this alone?

388
00:21:57,900 --> 00:21:59,192
[sighs softly]

389
00:21:59,193 --> 00:22:01,736
What are you all whispering about?

390
00:22:01,737 --> 00:22:04,740
- [door closes]
- You three look way too suspicious.

391
00:22:06,575 --> 00:22:09,119
Are you going to investigate
Jin Isoo's case?

392
00:22:10,204 --> 00:22:11,287
Hey,

393
00:22:11,288 --> 00:22:15,501
if you three make a move, don't you think
that will draw attention, huh?

394
00:22:17,586 --> 00:22:20,338
We'll look into it quietly.

395
00:22:20,339 --> 00:22:21,674
[♪ quirky music playing]

396
00:22:22,591 --> 00:22:23,592
[Junyoung] What?

397
00:22:24,552 --> 00:22:27,345
Hey, Jin Isoo may be a pain,
but at the end of the day,

398
00:22:27,346 --> 00:22:28,556
he's one of our own.

399
00:22:30,808 --> 00:22:33,226
Then, please get us the forensics report,

400
00:22:33,227 --> 00:22:36,814
the vehicle log at the time of the crime,
and the building's security footage.

401
00:22:37,398 --> 00:22:40,483
Oh, you always have a plan, Detective Joo.

402
00:22:40,484 --> 00:22:41,694
Okay, got it.

403
00:22:42,820 --> 00:22:45,071
Will you be able to manage all of that?

404
00:22:45,072 --> 00:22:46,782
What do you take me for, you punk?

405
00:22:47,491 --> 00:22:50,285
Do you know how many
connections I have in this field?

406
00:22:50,286 --> 00:22:51,704
In the world of police,

407
00:22:52,371 --> 00:22:53,706
I'm basically an influencer.

408
00:22:55,749 --> 00:22:56,792
[♪ music fades]

409
00:22:59,128 --> 00:23:00,211
[♪ foreboding music playing]

410
00:23:00,212 --> 00:23:01,672
We're from Internal Affairs.

411
00:23:02,548 --> 00:23:04,966
Senior Inspector Joo Hyera,
Inspector Park Junyoung,

412
00:23:04,967 --> 00:23:07,928
Senior Police Officer Choi Kyungjin.
Come with us.

413
00:23:22,443 --> 00:23:23,860
[♪ music swells, fades]

414
00:23:23,861 --> 00:23:27,072
Did you know
Detective Jin Isoo is a drug addict?

415
00:23:28,908 --> 00:23:29,991
No.

416
00:23:29,992 --> 00:23:31,618
Drugs were found in his system.

417
00:23:31,619 --> 00:23:32,995
A fairly large amount.

418
00:23:33,579 --> 00:23:36,623
How could you work with him and not know?

419
00:23:36,624 --> 00:23:37,999
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

420
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:39,083
[Kyungjin] <i>Drugs?</i>

421
00:23:39,084 --> 00:23:41,420
No. He'd never do such a thing.

422
00:23:42,087 --> 00:23:43,713
Someone must've drugged him.

423
00:23:43,714 --> 00:23:45,298
This was a setup!

424
00:23:45,299 --> 00:23:46,800
Anger-management issues?

425
00:23:47,551 --> 00:23:50,011
He arrested his half-brother,
who killed his parents.

426
00:23:50,012 --> 00:23:51,804
If it were me, I would've killed him.

427
00:23:51,805 --> 00:23:55,100
Then did you know
he was seeing a psychiatrist?

428
00:23:56,644 --> 00:23:57,852
No, I didn't know.

429
00:23:57,853 --> 00:24:01,774
After his mother was murdered, he was
receiving treatment for a very long time.

430
00:24:02,274 --> 00:24:03,566
You didn't know that either?

431
00:24:03,567 --> 00:24:05,152
I didn't know.

432
00:24:06,695 --> 00:24:07,821
Besides, that fact

433
00:24:08,614 --> 00:24:10,365
has nothing to do with this case.

434
00:24:10,366 --> 00:24:12,242
Why wouldn't it?

435
00:24:13,327 --> 00:24:16,579
I'm saying Jin Isoo is mentally ill.

436
00:24:16,580 --> 00:24:18,165
Please watch what you say.

437
00:24:18,749 --> 00:24:21,669
[inhales sharply] Maybe you knowingly
cleaned things up for him.

438
00:24:22,878 --> 00:24:24,045
He paid you, didn't he?

439
00:24:24,046 --> 00:24:25,047
[scoffs softly]

440
00:24:27,675 --> 00:24:28,676
No, he didn't.

441
00:24:29,343 --> 00:24:33,596
We'll be looking into your bank accounts,
so bear that in mind.

442
00:24:33,597 --> 00:24:35,014
[♪ gentle, somber music playing]

443
00:24:35,015 --> 00:24:36,350
What I really want to know

444
00:24:36,976 --> 00:24:38,768
is why Senior Inspector Joo Hyera,

445
00:24:38,769 --> 00:24:41,646
an elite officer who climbed
the ranks in record time,

446
00:24:41,647 --> 00:24:43,190
went to Gangha Police Station

447
00:24:43,983 --> 00:24:46,485
to play gofer for a chaebol.

448
00:24:47,403 --> 00:24:51,365
[inhales sharply] Did he promise you
a cushy job down the line?

449
00:24:52,032 --> 00:24:53,200
Jin Isoo

450
00:24:54,243 --> 00:24:57,162
is a capable and responsible detective.

451
00:25:00,541 --> 00:25:02,918
Someone who's narrow-minded

452
00:25:03,627 --> 00:25:04,962
won't be able to see that.

453
00:25:08,882 --> 00:25:09,925
[♪ music fades]

454
00:25:13,762 --> 00:25:15,054
EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR SEO JOOHEE

455
00:25:15,055 --> 00:25:16,348
EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR KIM JINSEO

456
00:25:16,974 --> 00:25:18,224
CHAIRMAN CHOI JEONGHUN

457
00:25:18,225 --> 00:25:19,392
PRESIDENT JIN MYUNGJAE

458
00:25:19,393 --> 00:25:20,685
BOARD CHAIR KUK MINGYUN

459
00:25:20,686 --> 00:25:22,646
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

460
00:25:43,917 --> 00:25:46,002
As you all know,

461
00:25:46,003 --> 00:25:48,505
Detective Jin Isoo was arrested
on a murder charge,

462
00:25:49,214 --> 00:25:51,425
so we have called
an emergency board meeting.

463
00:25:52,634 --> 00:25:54,428
Did he actually kill someone?

464
00:25:56,263 --> 00:25:57,848
It's still under investigation,

465
00:25:59,141 --> 00:26:00,893
but I don't believe he did.

466
00:26:01,602 --> 00:26:04,520
I'm not asking what you think, Chairman.

467
00:26:04,521 --> 00:26:09,275
Guilty or not, our company's reputation
is going to take a nosedive!

468
00:26:09,276 --> 00:26:14,323
The public is saying we're a company of
murderers owned by a family of murderers.

469
00:26:14,907 --> 00:26:17,784
Why did he have to go out there
to play detective, huh?

470
00:26:17,785 --> 00:26:20,495
He already caused trouble
with that bombing incident.

471
00:26:20,496 --> 00:26:23,624
You've known him since he was a child.
Didn't you see this coming?

472
00:26:24,666 --> 00:26:27,711
The Jin Isoo I know
would never do something like this.

473
00:26:28,712 --> 00:26:30,589
Until the investigation is concluded,

474
00:26:31,799 --> 00:26:33,091
I ask for your patience.

475
00:26:33,092 --> 00:26:37,095
How can you say that
when they have all the evidence?

476
00:26:37,096 --> 00:26:38,721
That's not all.

477
00:26:38,722 --> 00:26:42,433
Detective Jin Isoo used
Hansu Air Space's high-altitude UAV

478
00:26:42,434 --> 00:26:44,477
for personal purposes.

479
00:26:44,478 --> 00:26:45,938
[all murmuring]

480
00:26:47,981 --> 00:26:49,316
Did you know about this?

481
00:26:50,109 --> 00:26:51,110
Yes.

482
00:26:51,985 --> 00:26:53,694
I authorized it.

483
00:26:53,695 --> 00:26:55,113
What?

484
00:26:55,114 --> 00:26:57,156
[murmuring continues]

485
00:26:57,157 --> 00:26:58,158
[Mr. Choi] I apologize.

486
00:26:59,076 --> 00:27:00,660
What on earth...

487
00:27:00,661 --> 00:27:03,454
The press will be all over this.

488
00:27:03,455 --> 00:27:04,706
What are you going to do?

489
00:27:05,457 --> 00:27:06,542
It would seem

490
00:27:07,209 --> 00:27:10,378
we need someone to take responsibility.

491
00:27:10,379 --> 00:27:11,380
[♪ music swells]

492
00:27:13,882 --> 00:27:15,049
Please step down.

493
00:27:15,050 --> 00:27:16,134
[♪ music fades]

494
00:27:16,135 --> 00:27:18,594
I heard you're not even
in the best of health.

495
00:27:18,595 --> 00:27:20,430
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

496
00:27:25,269 --> 00:27:26,436
- [Mr. Choi clears throat]
- [♪ music fades]

497
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:33,694
- [Mingyun] Great job today.
- [IA investigator] You too.

498
00:27:38,323 --> 00:27:41,284
DETECTIVE DIVISION

499
00:27:41,285 --> 00:27:43,452
What's going to happen to Detective Jin?

500
00:27:43,453 --> 00:27:46,581
What do you think?
The case will go to prosecutors on Monday.

501
00:27:46,582 --> 00:27:47,707
What?

502
00:27:47,708 --> 00:27:50,084
You mean you already
concluded the investigation?

503
00:27:50,085 --> 00:27:53,254
The drugs, the weapon, the fingerprints.

504
00:27:53,255 --> 00:27:55,048
There's more than enough evidence.

505
00:27:55,757 --> 00:27:57,676
If Jin Isoo isn't the real culprit,

506
00:27:58,385 --> 00:27:59,720
if he was set up,

507
00:28:00,721 --> 00:28:02,388
how will you answer for this?

508
00:28:02,389 --> 00:28:04,390
I'll answer for it, in my own way.

509
00:28:04,391 --> 00:28:05,725
So you three

510
00:28:05,726 --> 00:28:08,811
should also answer
for all the crimes you've committed.

511
00:28:08,812 --> 00:28:10,354
[♪ tense music playing]

512
00:28:10,355 --> 00:28:11,815
Let's go.

513
00:28:12,357 --> 00:28:13,901
[♪ music increases in tempo]

514
00:28:17,696 --> 00:28:19,071
[keys jingling]

515
00:28:19,072 --> 00:28:20,156
[♪ music fades]

516
00:28:20,157 --> 00:28:21,490
[lock clicks open]

517
00:28:21,491 --> 00:28:22,534
[gate latch clanks]

518
00:28:24,328 --> 00:28:26,163
Mr. Jin Isoo, you have a visitor.

519
00:28:35,839 --> 00:28:36,840
Isoo!

520
00:28:39,051 --> 00:28:40,551
What are you doing here?

521
00:28:40,552 --> 00:28:43,095
I was worried about you.

522
00:28:43,096 --> 00:28:44,431
What on earth happened?

523
00:28:51,229 --> 00:28:52,648
Did you really

524
00:28:53,482 --> 00:28:55,525
kill Younghwan?

525
00:28:56,610 --> 00:28:57,986
No, I didn't.

526
00:29:00,113 --> 00:29:01,405
Are you sure you didn't?

527
00:29:01,406 --> 00:29:03,492
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

528
00:29:12,376 --> 00:29:13,377
I had a feeling

529
00:29:14,419 --> 00:29:16,046
this day would come.

530
00:29:17,589 --> 00:29:19,424
From the first day I met you.

531
00:29:22,928 --> 00:29:24,137
And about Seungju.

532
00:29:24,972 --> 00:29:29,101
I couldn't understand
why you didn't kill him.

533
00:29:29,935 --> 00:29:31,395
He murdered your parents.

534
00:29:32,062 --> 00:29:35,065
You probably had
plenty of opportunities to kill him.

535
00:29:39,361 --> 00:29:40,862
What are you talking about?

536
00:29:42,906 --> 00:29:44,448
I'm not like you.

537
00:29:44,449 --> 00:29:45,534
Are you sure?

538
00:29:46,994 --> 00:29:49,037
Weren't you holding back all this time?

539
00:29:50,664 --> 00:29:52,833
Then you took it all out on Younghwan.

540
00:29:54,835 --> 00:29:56,086
Think back carefully.

541
00:29:56,837 --> 00:30:00,674
Remember how good it felt
when you stabbed Younghwan.

542
00:30:01,425 --> 00:30:02,926
That's who you are.

543
00:30:04,886 --> 00:30:06,346
Stop talking nonsense and go.

544
00:30:06,930 --> 00:30:08,056
[thud]

545
00:30:11,643 --> 00:30:12,894
Don't run away from this.

546
00:30:15,313 --> 00:30:18,567
Once you accept it,
you'll finally be free.

547
00:30:24,114 --> 00:30:27,576
After all, you're my Little Prince.

548
00:30:35,042 --> 00:30:36,043
[♪ music fades]

549
00:30:40,130 --> 00:30:41,881
[Byungsik] This guy, Kim Younghwan.

550
00:30:41,882 --> 00:30:45,009
He didn't do much
after he was released from prison.

551
00:30:45,010 --> 00:30:46,802
And the security footage?

552
00:30:46,803 --> 00:30:48,096
Here you go.

553
00:30:48,930 --> 00:30:50,723
And this is the forensics report.

554
00:30:50,724 --> 00:30:52,391
CRIME SCENE FORENSICS REPORT

555
00:30:52,392 --> 00:30:54,769
And here's the list of vehicles.

556
00:30:54,770 --> 00:30:57,021
You got these really quickly. Thank you.

557
00:30:57,022 --> 00:31:00,442
We should get Jin Isoo out of there.
He grew up pampered.

558
00:31:01,068 --> 00:31:03,194
I bet he's crying right about now.

559
00:31:03,195 --> 00:31:04,446
[chuckles softly]

560
00:31:07,282 --> 00:31:08,325
[gate latch clanks]

561
00:31:11,828 --> 00:31:13,497
[inmate exhales, sniffles]

562
00:31:14,873 --> 00:31:15,874
[groans softly]

563
00:31:16,625 --> 00:31:17,667
[gate clicks]

564
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:20,169
[gate latch clanks]

565
00:31:20,170 --> 00:31:21,755
- [keys jingle]
- [lock clicks]

566
00:31:22,964 --> 00:31:25,674
Excuse me, sir. Sir!

567
00:31:25,675 --> 00:31:27,134
Can I get something to eat?

568
00:31:27,135 --> 00:31:29,346
I'm starving to death!

569
00:31:30,013 --> 00:31:31,473
You're so mean.

570
00:31:32,599 --> 00:31:33,682
[sniffles sharply]

571
00:31:33,683 --> 00:31:34,767
[exhales softly]

572
00:31:34,768 --> 00:31:35,769
[sniffles sharply]

573
00:31:37,437 --> 00:31:38,480
Jin Isoo.

574
00:31:39,397 --> 00:31:40,481
Flex Cop.

575
00:31:40,482 --> 00:31:41,565
[♪ quirky, suspenseful music playing]

576
00:31:41,566 --> 00:31:42,567
Ah, yes.

577
00:31:44,027 --> 00:31:47,113
Wow. It's great to meet you. I follow you.

578
00:31:47,114 --> 00:31:48,907
Can I get a photo with you?

579
00:31:50,200 --> 00:31:51,535
[laughs heartily]

580
00:31:53,078 --> 00:31:55,080
I don't have my phone.

581
00:31:55,789 --> 00:31:58,082
Sir! Can I borrow your phone?

582
00:31:58,083 --> 00:32:00,001
- To take a picture.
- [guard] Be quiet.

583
00:32:00,794 --> 00:32:02,379
You're so mean.

584
00:32:03,505 --> 00:32:06,675
Bro, then I suppose we could at least...

585
00:32:07,759 --> 00:32:08,760
Let's hug.

586
00:32:13,682 --> 00:32:15,517
[muffled] One second. [sniffles softly]

587
00:32:16,101 --> 00:32:17,769
[gags, retching]

588
00:32:20,438 --> 00:32:21,522
[exhales heavily]

589
00:32:21,523 --> 00:32:22,606
[slurping]

590
00:32:22,607 --> 00:32:23,774
[♪ music fades]

591
00:32:23,775 --> 00:32:26,027
You can still eat
after throwing up like that?

592
00:32:26,444 --> 00:32:28,530
[exhales contentedly] The drugs wore off.

593
00:32:30,115 --> 00:32:31,741
Are you in here for doing drugs?

594
00:32:33,577 --> 00:32:35,744
I can't really remember.

595
00:32:35,745 --> 00:32:38,081
I was having a great time in a club,

596
00:32:38,999 --> 00:32:40,583
and I felt a bit hot,

597
00:32:40,584 --> 00:32:43,002
then they found me on a swing, butt naked.

598
00:32:43,003 --> 00:32:44,379
[chuckling]

599
00:32:45,755 --> 00:32:47,089
By any chance,

600
00:32:47,090 --> 00:32:49,800
do you know a drug
that can be absorbed through the skin?

601
00:32:49,801 --> 00:32:51,468
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

602
00:32:51,469 --> 00:32:52,888
There's Ruby.

603
00:32:53,847 --> 00:32:56,223
There's also "Touch."
Just by holding it like this,

604
00:32:56,224 --> 00:32:57,641
it gives you an instant kick.

605
00:32:57,642 --> 00:32:59,685
But it's super potent.

606
00:32:59,686 --> 00:33:02,147
That stuff is nasty.

607
00:33:03,106 --> 00:33:04,773
But I don't do that kind of stuff.

608
00:33:04,774 --> 00:33:06,902
If you use that drug for the first time,

609
00:33:07,444 --> 00:33:08,653
can it make you violent?

610
00:33:09,404 --> 00:33:11,114
That's usually what happens.

611
00:33:12,199 --> 00:33:15,576
How should I put this?
People with all those pent-up emotions,

612
00:33:15,577 --> 00:33:18,622
with a lot of negative feelings
end up causing trouble.

613
00:33:19,372 --> 00:33:20,373
The truth is,

614
00:33:20,957 --> 00:33:22,374
when I first did it,

615
00:33:22,375 --> 00:33:25,754
I broke all these windows
and caused a huge scene.

616
00:33:28,757 --> 00:33:29,758
But, bro,

617
00:33:30,967 --> 00:33:33,135
did you do drugs and do something bad?

618
00:33:33,136 --> 00:33:34,346
[♪ music swells]

619
00:33:40,477 --> 00:33:41,686
[♪ music fades]

620
00:33:43,647 --> 00:33:45,565
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

621
00:33:52,572 --> 00:33:54,866
[Younghwan] <i>Jin Isoo. Enjoy the fall.</i>

622
00:33:57,202 --> 00:33:59,495
[Younghwan laughing maniacally]

623
00:33:59,496 --> 00:34:00,622
[audio distorts]

624
00:34:10,507 --> 00:34:12,259
[♪ music swells]

625
00:34:13,260 --> 00:34:15,427
[high-pitched tone droning]

626
00:34:15,428 --> 00:34:17,347
[♪ eerie, suspenseful music playing]

627
00:34:21,643 --> 00:34:22,810
[squelch]

628
00:34:22,811 --> 00:34:24,145
[muffled metallic clinking]

629
00:34:25,981 --> 00:34:27,565
[metallic clinking intensifies]

630
00:34:28,608 --> 00:34:30,567
[inmate] What's wrong? Come on, breathe!

631
00:34:30,568 --> 00:34:31,694
[audio normalizes]

632
00:34:31,695 --> 00:34:32,778
Breathe!

633
00:34:32,779 --> 00:34:34,239
[Isoo breathing heavily]

634
00:34:35,198 --> 00:34:36,658
Are you okay?

635
00:34:40,996 --> 00:34:42,789
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

636
00:34:45,875 --> 00:34:47,419
FORENSIC CHEMISTRY REPORT

637
00:34:51,715 --> 00:34:55,342
[Isoo, over recording] <i>Hello?
Please get the police here.</i>

638
00:34:55,343 --> 00:34:57,928
<i>I killed someone.</i>

639
00:34:57,929 --> 00:34:59,680
<i>Jin Isoo.</i>

640
00:34:59,681 --> 00:35:00,932
[mouse clicks]

641
00:35:02,392 --> 00:35:05,811
<i>Hello? Please get the police here.</i>

642
00:35:05,812 --> 00:35:07,187
<i>I killed...</i>

643
00:35:07,188 --> 00:35:09,190
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

644
00:35:10,191 --> 00:35:12,360
FORENSIC REPORT
NAME: KIM YOUNGHWAN

645
00:35:14,821 --> 00:35:18,700
[Hyera] <i>The initial stabbing is believed
to have been near the foot of the stairs.</i>

646
00:35:19,701 --> 00:35:21,368
<i>A 5 cm stab wound to the left chest,</i>

647
00:35:21,369 --> 00:35:24,330
<i>2 cm and 4 cm stab wounds
to the left abdomen,</i>

648
00:35:24,331 --> 00:35:27,166
<i>along with defensive wounds
to the left palm.</i>

649
00:35:27,167 --> 00:35:30,419
<i>Defensive wounds on the chest,
abdomen, and hand were found.</i>

650
00:35:30,420 --> 00:35:32,047
- [Younghwan grunts]
- [squelching]

651
00:35:33,340 --> 00:35:34,424
[groans]

652
00:35:36,217 --> 00:35:39,429
[Hyera] <i>The marks suggest
the victim crawled unaided.</i>

653
00:35:40,013 --> 00:35:41,014
[grunts]

654
00:35:41,890 --> 00:35:43,140
- [squelch]
- [Younghwan exclaims]

655
00:35:43,141 --> 00:35:45,268
[Hyera] <i>A 3 cm stab wound
was found on the back.</i>

656
00:35:46,102 --> 00:35:49,272
<i>The victim is believed to have died from
blood loss caused by multiple stab wounds.</i>

657
00:35:51,816 --> 00:35:56,570
<i>Approximately 2.4 m from the resting point
near the stairs to the sofa,</i>

658
00:35:56,571 --> 00:36:00,574
<i>smear marks believed to be
evidence of dragging were found.</i>

659
00:36:00,575 --> 00:36:02,118
[♪ music increases in tempo]

660
00:36:05,372 --> 00:36:06,455
[killer grunts]

661
00:36:06,456 --> 00:36:07,791
[♪ music resumes tempo]

662
00:36:11,586 --> 00:36:12,587
[♪ music fades]

663
00:36:14,756 --> 00:36:15,839
[sighs softly]

664
00:36:15,840 --> 00:36:17,926
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

665
00:36:29,979 --> 00:36:31,523
[doorbell chiming]

666
00:36:35,485 --> 00:36:36,860
[doorbell chiming]

667
00:36:36,861 --> 00:36:38,196
[knocking at door]

668
00:36:39,114 --> 00:36:41,366
[Hyera, over monitor]
<i>I'm with the police. Is anyone home?</i>

669
00:36:47,831 --> 00:36:49,832
- [softly] Oh!
- [♪ music resumes tempo]

670
00:36:49,833 --> 00:36:51,084
Show me your ID.

671
00:36:54,671 --> 00:36:55,921
PUBLIC OFFICIAL ID
JOO HYERA

672
00:36:55,922 --> 00:36:57,965
- Are you really a police officer?
- [♪ music fades]

673
00:36:57,966 --> 00:36:59,843
Yes, I really am.

674
00:37:01,261 --> 00:37:02,262
Come in.

675
00:37:17,235 --> 00:37:18,236
Are you a singer?

676
00:37:19,154 --> 00:37:20,362
Oh... [chuckles]

677
00:37:20,363 --> 00:37:22,698
Yes, that's right. I'm Ko Danbi.

678
00:37:22,699 --> 00:37:23,700
Ah.

679
00:37:25,118 --> 00:37:28,580
Do you know about the incident
that happened next door a few days ago?

680
00:37:29,247 --> 00:37:30,497
I do.

681
00:37:30,498 --> 00:37:33,250
I finally found this house,
but now I have to move again.

682
00:37:33,251 --> 00:37:35,670
[sighs] I don't feel safe
living here anymore.

683
00:37:37,130 --> 00:37:39,214
But why are you handling it like this?

684
00:37:39,215 --> 00:37:42,301
- Sorry?
- I mean, Jin Isoo isn't the killer.

685
00:37:42,302 --> 00:37:43,385
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

686
00:37:43,386 --> 00:37:44,804
What are you talking about?

687
00:37:45,472 --> 00:37:47,766
Someone else went into that house. A man.

688
00:37:50,018 --> 00:37:51,519
How do you know that?

689
00:37:52,854 --> 00:37:55,565
You know what happened
to me last year, right?

690
00:37:56,983 --> 00:37:58,233
Uh... [chuckles]

691
00:37:58,234 --> 00:37:59,693
I'm afraid I don't.

692
00:37:59,694 --> 00:38:00,862
Oh...

693
00:38:01,529 --> 00:38:03,531
I guess you don't read celebrity gossip.

694
00:38:04,991 --> 00:38:08,452
There was this crazy stalker
who was obsessed with me last year.

695
00:38:08,453 --> 00:38:11,872
He hid in the stairwell
every day and watched me,

696
00:38:11,873 --> 00:38:13,708
then eventually broke into my house.

697
00:38:14,459 --> 00:38:17,753
I came home after a performance
to find him lying on my bed.

698
00:38:17,754 --> 00:38:20,547
I moved here because I heard
it was the safest place around,

699
00:38:20,548 --> 00:38:22,008
but I couldn't sleep anymore.

700
00:38:22,550 --> 00:38:25,469
After that, I became an alcoholic.

701
00:38:25,470 --> 00:38:28,765
I'm on medication for anxiety,
and I haven't been able to perform.

702
00:38:29,974 --> 00:38:34,020
[sighs heavily]
It's really easy to ruin someone's life.

703
00:38:36,189 --> 00:38:38,941
But about you seeing someone...

704
00:38:38,942 --> 00:38:40,192
Ah.

705
00:38:40,193 --> 00:38:41,903
There's a sensor in front of my door.

706
00:38:43,530 --> 00:38:45,865
My intercom monitor turns on
when someone walks by.

707
00:38:46,324 --> 00:38:47,491
[monitor beeping]

708
00:38:47,492 --> 00:38:49,202
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

709
00:39:00,922 --> 00:39:02,589
<i>Around 30 minutes later...</i>

710
00:39:02,590 --> 00:39:03,757
[monitor beeping]

711
00:39:03,758 --> 00:39:05,510
<i>...some guy walked past.</i>

712
00:39:08,137 --> 00:39:09,138
[slurps]

713
00:39:11,182 --> 00:39:12,767
[♪ music increases in tempo]

714
00:39:15,687 --> 00:39:16,813
[♪ music swells]

715
00:39:17,605 --> 00:39:18,689
[♪ music fades]

716
00:39:18,690 --> 00:39:21,401
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY

717
00:39:22,110 --> 00:39:23,694
Your hair isn't looking so great.

718
00:39:23,695 --> 00:39:25,613
I didn't wash it.

719
00:39:26,239 --> 00:39:28,616
[chuckles softly] Are you at least eating?

720
00:39:29,868 --> 00:39:31,743
I don't have an appetite.

721
00:39:31,744 --> 00:39:33,370
You should still eat something.

722
00:39:33,371 --> 00:39:35,373
Why do you look so down?

723
00:39:36,040 --> 00:39:37,791
I'm just not used to this place yet.

724
00:39:37,792 --> 00:39:39,919
Why get used to it?
You'll be coming out soon.

725
00:39:41,254 --> 00:39:43,506
The Metropolitan Unit didn't
investigate properly.

726
00:39:46,259 --> 00:39:49,512
In their eyes... [sighs]
...I probably look guilty.

727
00:39:51,055 --> 00:39:52,140
The truth is,

728
00:39:54,309 --> 00:39:55,935
I'm on psychiatric medication.

729
00:39:57,353 --> 00:39:58,354
I know.

730
00:39:59,647 --> 00:40:00,857
You have panic disorder.

731
00:40:02,650 --> 00:40:03,776
If, by some chance,

732
00:40:05,612 --> 00:40:07,614
I really did kill him...

733
00:40:08,573 --> 00:40:09,698
[Hyera] Hey.

734
00:40:09,699 --> 00:40:11,200
Snap out of it.

735
00:40:12,368 --> 00:40:14,621
A few days in lockup
and you've gone all pathetic.

736
00:40:16,623 --> 00:40:17,832
Well, I mean,

737
00:40:19,334 --> 00:40:21,461
I'm not exactly
the most trustworthy person.

738
00:40:22,170 --> 00:40:23,421
Why not?

739
00:40:24,130 --> 00:40:25,590
I trust you.

740
00:40:26,799 --> 00:40:29,886
We believe you're innocent,
and we're still investigating the case.

741
00:40:35,058 --> 00:40:36,726
After you went home,

742
00:40:37,435 --> 00:40:39,227
a man entered your house.

743
00:40:39,228 --> 00:40:40,729
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

744
00:40:40,730 --> 00:40:41,813
A man?

745
00:40:41,814 --> 00:40:43,524
Your neighbor's camera caught him.

746
00:40:45,026 --> 00:40:48,321
You were drugged, then he went inside
and killed Kim Younghwan.

747
00:40:49,906 --> 00:40:51,448
[exhales incredulously]

748
00:40:51,449 --> 00:40:52,909
Are you going to snap out of it?

749
00:40:54,202 --> 00:40:55,203
Yeah.

750
00:40:57,372 --> 00:40:59,916
You just think about
what the killer's after.

751
00:41:01,250 --> 00:41:04,587
Who and why would someone do this?

752
00:41:05,922 --> 00:41:09,217
They could've just killed you,
but put you in here instead.

753
00:41:11,719 --> 00:41:12,720
Okay.

754
00:41:13,846 --> 00:41:15,222
Ah.

755
00:41:15,223 --> 00:41:17,224
Yu Seongwon came here.

756
00:41:17,225 --> 00:41:18,893
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

757
00:41:20,144 --> 00:41:21,145
Yu Seongwon?

758
00:41:22,021 --> 00:41:23,022
Why?

759
00:41:24,065 --> 00:41:25,066
I don't know.

760
00:41:26,317 --> 00:41:28,486
He told me to accept
that this is who I am.

761
00:41:30,154 --> 00:41:34,491
He looked happy that I was a murderer.

762
00:41:34,492 --> 00:41:35,909
[♪ music increases in tempo]

763
00:41:35,910 --> 00:41:37,036
Could this be

764
00:41:38,121 --> 00:41:40,415
Yu Seongwon's doing?

765
00:41:42,417 --> 00:41:43,626
Yu Seongwon?

766
00:41:46,337 --> 00:41:47,421
Why would he?

767
00:41:47,422 --> 00:41:48,548
[♪ music swells]

768
00:41:52,593 --> 00:41:53,803
[♪ music fades]

769
00:41:55,346 --> 00:41:56,471
[mouse clicks]

770
00:41:56,472 --> 00:41:57,765
[doorbell chiming]

771
00:42:02,020 --> 00:42:03,021
Hyera.

772
00:42:04,981 --> 00:42:06,064
Coffee?

773
00:42:06,065 --> 00:42:08,151
[chuckles softly]
In the middle of the night?

774
00:42:12,280 --> 00:42:14,073
What happened with Detective Jin?

775
00:42:16,534 --> 00:42:17,618
[sighs heavily]

776
00:42:18,244 --> 00:42:19,787
We're still looking into it.

777
00:42:21,789 --> 00:42:24,125
I think he was set up.

778
00:42:25,960 --> 00:42:27,419
[inhales sharply]

779
00:42:27,420 --> 00:42:29,129
Just maybe,

780
00:42:29,130 --> 00:42:30,798
could it have been Yu Seongwon?

781
00:42:31,507 --> 00:42:33,009
- Yu Seongwon?
- Yes.

782
00:42:34,177 --> 00:42:35,762
When he found our cameras,

783
00:42:36,763 --> 00:42:39,891
what if he realized Isoo was on our side
and set the whole thing up?

784
00:42:41,350 --> 00:42:43,852
But he hasn't moved
since breaking our cameras.

785
00:42:43,853 --> 00:42:44,854
Really?

786
00:42:47,899 --> 00:42:49,775
I heard he came to see Jin Isoo.

787
00:42:49,776 --> 00:42:51,860
I followed him that time.

788
00:42:51,861 --> 00:42:54,112
I put a tracker on his car.

789
00:42:54,113 --> 00:42:55,655
[engine roaring]

790
00:42:55,656 --> 00:42:57,241
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

791
00:43:03,331 --> 00:43:04,707
[♪ music swells]

792
00:43:08,711 --> 00:43:10,004
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY

793
00:43:12,924 --> 00:43:14,800
YU SEONGWON
STUDIO

794
00:43:14,801 --> 00:43:16,010
[♪ music fades]

795
00:43:19,555 --> 00:43:20,556
What's that?

796
00:43:21,933 --> 00:43:23,225
Ah...

797
00:43:23,226 --> 00:43:27,104
After Detective Jin was arrested,
the high-altitude UAV got disconnected.

798
00:43:27,105 --> 00:43:28,980
- I guess they found out.
- So?

799
00:43:28,981 --> 00:43:31,691
Yours truly went in the middle
of the night to install it.

800
00:43:31,692 --> 00:43:33,611
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

801
00:43:41,202 --> 00:43:43,120
VIEWCAM

802
00:43:43,121 --> 00:43:45,122
- Why didn't you tell me?
- [♪ music fades]

803
00:43:45,123 --> 00:43:46,499
I figured you'd be busy.

804
00:43:47,750 --> 00:43:49,835
I can handle this much on my own.

805
00:43:49,836 --> 00:43:50,837
[scoffs]

806
00:43:52,463 --> 00:43:54,464
You're really on the ball now.

807
00:43:54,465 --> 00:43:56,424
I'm a one-man operation.

808
00:43:56,425 --> 00:43:57,510
[Minjae chuckles]

809
00:43:57,969 --> 00:44:00,470
Anyway, what did Yu Seongwon say to him?

810
00:44:00,471 --> 00:44:02,806
That he knew Jin Isoo would commit murder.

811
00:44:02,807 --> 00:44:03,974
[♪ ominous music playing]

812
00:44:03,975 --> 00:44:05,059
He found it amusing.

813
00:44:05,768 --> 00:44:07,019
What do you mean?

814
00:44:07,812 --> 00:44:10,689
That's why I thought
maybe Yu Seongwon was behind this.

815
00:44:10,690 --> 00:44:13,150
But this isn't how he does things.

816
00:44:13,151 --> 00:44:15,278
He kidnaps people and kills them.

817
00:44:17,530 --> 00:44:21,242
What does Jin Isoo mean to Yu Seongwon?

818
00:44:22,368 --> 00:44:23,869
That's what I don't get.

819
00:44:23,870 --> 00:44:25,328
You're right.

820
00:44:25,329 --> 00:44:28,082
I think Isoo does mean
something special to him.

821
00:44:29,458 --> 00:44:30,543
[♪ music fades]

822
00:44:31,586 --> 00:44:32,920
What are you going to do now?

823
00:44:34,088 --> 00:44:36,506
We have a suspect,
so we'll have to catch him first.

824
00:44:36,507 --> 00:44:38,175
Call me if you need anything.

825
00:44:38,176 --> 00:44:41,345
[chuckles] Okay. Call me
if anything happens with Yu Seongwon.

826
00:44:42,889 --> 00:44:44,432
Don't act alone again.

827
00:44:45,057 --> 00:44:46,558
Okay, I got it.

828
00:44:46,559 --> 00:44:47,643
[chuckles softly]

829
00:44:49,437 --> 00:44:56,652
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE

830
00:44:58,237 --> 00:45:00,740
DETECTIVE UNIT 1

831
00:45:01,407 --> 00:45:03,868
[detectives chattering, laughing]

832
00:45:07,246 --> 00:45:10,832
[sighs] What do you want this early?
Don't you have work to do?

833
00:45:10,833 --> 00:45:12,752
We came to save you.

834
00:45:14,212 --> 00:45:17,255
You haven't turned Jin Isoo over
to the prosecutors yet, right?

835
00:45:17,256 --> 00:45:18,340
[scoffs]

836
00:45:18,341 --> 00:45:20,592
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

837
00:45:20,593 --> 00:45:22,844
Thirty minutes after
Detective Jin went inside,

838
00:45:22,845 --> 00:45:25,347
this man went toward his house.

839
00:45:25,348 --> 00:45:27,850
He was caught on the neighbor's camera.

840
00:45:28,643 --> 00:45:30,727
So what? What about this man?

841
00:45:30,728 --> 00:45:32,062
He's a suspect.

842
00:45:32,063 --> 00:45:35,232
I'm saying it's possible
that this man killed Kim Younghwan.

843
00:45:35,233 --> 00:45:36,317
[scoffs]

844
00:45:37,068 --> 00:45:38,735
Are you serious?

845
00:45:38,736 --> 00:45:40,988
How will you prove
that this guy killed him?

846
00:45:42,323 --> 00:45:43,573
We can if we catch him.

847
00:45:43,574 --> 00:45:44,659
[sighs heavily]

848
00:45:45,201 --> 00:45:47,953
Either way, it's true
that Jin Isoo did drugs.

849
00:45:47,954 --> 00:45:51,082
This guy might've been called
to clean up after him.

850
00:45:52,250 --> 00:45:53,417
[Junyoung] That drug

851
00:45:54,210 --> 00:45:57,128
was applied to Detective Jin's hand
by the victim.

852
00:45:57,129 --> 00:45:58,297
[♪ music fades]

853
00:45:59,757 --> 00:46:01,676
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music resumes]

854
00:46:03,511 --> 00:46:05,136
It's a drug called "Touch."

855
00:46:05,137 --> 00:46:07,222
<i>It absorbs right away through the skin,</i>

856
00:46:07,223 --> 00:46:09,182
<i>and Detective Jin was drugged that way.</i>

857
00:46:09,183 --> 00:46:10,184
[camera shutter clicks]

858
00:46:11,269 --> 00:46:13,812
<i>Traces of Touch was found
on the victim's hand.</i>

859
00:46:13,813 --> 00:46:15,731
[camera shutter clicking]

860
00:46:18,317 --> 00:46:19,902
As for the call that came in,

861
00:46:20,653 --> 00:46:23,071
I guess you're not
very familiar with this.

862
00:46:23,072 --> 00:46:25,283
Please listen to it again, carefully.

863
00:46:27,702 --> 00:46:28,868
[♪ music fades]

864
00:46:28,869 --> 00:46:30,287
[Isoo, over recording] <i>Hello?</i>

865
00:46:30,288 --> 00:46:32,497
<i>Please get the police here.</i>

866
00:46:32,498 --> 00:46:34,541
<i>I killed someone.</i>

867
00:46:34,542 --> 00:46:36,460
<i>Jin Isoo.</i>

868
00:46:37,211 --> 00:46:39,839
<i>I'm at my house.</i>

869
00:46:40,589 --> 00:46:42,173
I know. I heard it all.

870
00:46:42,174 --> 00:46:44,718
[exclaims] You don't know.

871
00:46:44,719 --> 00:46:47,178
When you record something,
even if it sounds silent,

872
00:46:47,179 --> 00:46:48,763
it still captures "room tone,"

873
00:46:48,764 --> 00:46:51,182
which is like the hum of a fridge.

874
00:46:51,183 --> 00:46:52,350
But it's not there.

875
00:46:52,351 --> 00:46:54,227
[♪ quirky, dramatic music playing]

876
00:46:54,228 --> 00:46:55,520
In other words, it's fake.

877
00:46:55,521 --> 00:46:58,816
Software's so good these days
that it only takes three minutes to make.

878
00:47:03,696 --> 00:47:05,196
So what?

879
00:47:05,197 --> 00:47:07,533
We've identified the suspect.

880
00:47:08,367 --> 00:47:09,910
If the real killer is caught,

881
00:47:10,870 --> 00:47:11,953
what will happen?

882
00:47:11,954 --> 00:47:14,748
[Kyungjin, clears throat]
The press will have a field day.

883
00:47:14,749 --> 00:47:17,417
That's going to be
really embarrassing for you.

884
00:47:17,418 --> 00:47:20,045
Hansu Group won't just stand by.
They'll sue right away.

885
00:47:20,046 --> 00:47:22,006
Their reputation took a nosedive.

886
00:47:23,049 --> 00:47:24,883
[Kyungjin] That aside,
I'm worried about Isoo.

887
00:47:24,884 --> 00:47:26,760
I bet he's really angry.

888
00:47:26,761 --> 00:47:28,762
I'd lose it, too.

889
00:47:28,763 --> 00:47:31,849
- That would give anyone anger issues.
- [Kyungjin sighs]

890
00:47:33,476 --> 00:47:35,561
I told you I would save you.

891
00:47:36,854 --> 00:47:40,316
I can't do anything about you
facing disciplinary action for negligence,

892
00:47:41,317 --> 00:47:45,404
but I can stop Detective Jin
and Hansu Group from suing you.

893
00:47:47,281 --> 00:47:48,491
[sighs in exasperation]

894
00:47:50,159 --> 00:47:51,577
Please release Jin Isoo.

895
00:47:56,415 --> 00:47:57,416
[♪ music fades]

896
00:48:03,255 --> 00:48:04,757
What's taking so long?

897
00:48:06,384 --> 00:48:09,470
I'm sure Detective Kang is busy
making excuses left and right.

898
00:48:12,890 --> 00:48:13,891
Bro!

899
00:48:14,433 --> 00:48:16,227
[♪ gentle, poignant music playing]

900
00:48:19,688 --> 00:48:20,940
[exhales contentedly]

901
00:48:21,941 --> 00:48:23,566
Did you get out after 10 years?

902
00:48:23,567 --> 00:48:25,485
That's just how I feel.

903
00:48:25,486 --> 00:48:26,903
One day felt like a decade.

904
00:48:26,904 --> 00:48:28,154
[chuckles softly]

905
00:48:28,155 --> 00:48:29,365
You made it through.

906
00:48:30,491 --> 00:48:31,492
Here.

907
00:48:35,663 --> 00:48:37,288
PUBLIC OFFICIAL ID
JIN ISOO

908
00:48:37,289 --> 00:48:38,457
Let's go.

909
00:48:39,375 --> 00:48:40,750
Where are we going?

910
00:48:40,751 --> 00:48:41,918
[Kyungjin] To celebrate.

911
00:48:41,919 --> 00:48:43,044
Celebrating your release.

912
00:48:43,045 --> 00:48:45,713
Ah, not your release,
but for not getting charged.

913
00:48:45,714 --> 00:48:46,881
[scoffs softly]

914
00:48:46,882 --> 00:48:47,883
Let's go, bro.

915
00:48:48,717 --> 00:48:50,135
Don't link arms like this.

916
00:48:50,136 --> 00:48:52,680
- I've been traumatized. Let go.
- [♪ music fades]

917
00:48:53,681 --> 00:48:56,433
Mmm. Mix in the truffle like this.

918
00:48:56,434 --> 00:48:58,269
[exclaims] Mmm!

919
00:48:58,894 --> 00:49:00,062
Hey, slow down.

920
00:49:00,729 --> 00:49:03,231
I haven't eaten in three days.
Look at my hollow eyes.

921
00:49:03,232 --> 00:49:06,860
Isn't it nice, being together like this
and enjoying good food, mmm?

922
00:49:06,861 --> 00:49:07,862
Eat up.

923
00:49:08,487 --> 00:49:09,613
- [sighs deeply]
- [Isoo] Mmm!

924
00:49:12,032 --> 00:49:13,033
[Hyera] Here.

925
00:49:14,994 --> 00:49:15,995
Eat more.

926
00:49:17,830 --> 00:49:19,164
What's this?

927
00:49:19,165 --> 00:49:20,790
Why are you being so nice?

928
00:49:20,791 --> 00:49:22,375
Fine, then don't.

929
00:49:22,376 --> 00:49:23,668
Detective Park, eat up.

930
00:49:23,669 --> 00:49:25,378
Yes, thank you.

931
00:49:25,379 --> 00:49:27,088
This truffle aroma is amazing.

932
00:49:27,089 --> 00:49:30,176
Hey! Give it here. It's mine.

933
00:49:31,135 --> 00:49:33,052
[Kyungjin, grunts]
There's so many people here.

934
00:49:33,053 --> 00:49:34,804
It's become really popular now.

935
00:49:34,805 --> 00:49:36,055
Where did you run off to?

936
00:49:36,056 --> 00:49:37,057
Bro.

937
00:49:38,726 --> 00:49:39,976
Ta-da!

938
00:49:39,977 --> 00:49:41,102
What are you doing?

939
00:49:41,103 --> 00:49:43,021
Just have one bite.
It's bad luck otherwise.

940
00:49:43,022 --> 00:49:44,106
Hey, hey!

941
00:49:45,024 --> 00:49:47,318
I'm already a lucky guy. Super lucky.

942
00:49:48,110 --> 00:49:49,527
- No way.
- Just one bite.

943
00:49:49,528 --> 00:49:50,778
- No!
- Just one bite.

944
00:49:50,779 --> 00:49:52,030
- Open up. Ah...
- [Isoo] Seriously.

945
00:49:52,031 --> 00:49:53,531
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

946
00:49:53,532 --> 00:49:55,283
You have some, too. Just to be safe.

947
00:49:55,284 --> 00:49:58,036
Eat it as a precaution.
Have more. There you go.

948
00:49:58,037 --> 00:49:59,245
[♪ music fades]

949
00:49:59,246 --> 00:50:01,040
[Hyera] We found the suspect. [sighs]

950
00:50:04,043 --> 00:50:05,502
Cho Pilgu.

951
00:50:05,503 --> 00:50:06,753
Do you know him?

952
00:50:06,754 --> 00:50:09,506
No. How did you find him?

953
00:50:09,507 --> 00:50:12,258
He's a professional. Four prior
convictions, assault and murder.

954
00:50:12,259 --> 00:50:13,676
He's extremely methodical.

955
00:50:13,677 --> 00:50:17,305
He left by subway, so we spent all night
checking footage from all the stations.

956
00:50:17,306 --> 00:50:20,016
He's the one who killed Kim Younghwan.

957
00:50:20,017 --> 00:50:21,477
[♪ tense, pulsating music playing]

958
00:50:23,020 --> 00:50:24,479
[phone clinks]

959
00:50:24,480 --> 00:50:25,981
We'll have to catch him first.

960
00:50:26,607 --> 00:50:28,525
- Stakeout starts tomorrow.
- Got it.

961
00:50:28,526 --> 00:50:30,277
- [in English] Okay. [in Korean] Cheers.
- Got it.

962
00:50:30,861 --> 00:50:32,238
- [Isoo grunts]
- [clinking]

963
00:50:33,280 --> 00:50:34,323
[♪ music fades]

964
00:50:34,907 --> 00:50:35,908
Tomorrow?

965
00:50:37,868 --> 00:50:38,911
All right.

966
00:50:40,663 --> 00:50:41,664
[Isoo] Honk, honk.

967
00:50:44,375 --> 00:50:45,834
Why do you look so serious?

968
00:50:46,210 --> 00:50:47,418
[sighs in relief]

969
00:50:47,419 --> 00:50:49,921
I heard you were released today.

970
00:50:49,922 --> 00:50:51,006
You knew?

971
00:50:51,674 --> 00:50:54,134
Then you should've come with some tofu.

972
00:50:55,010 --> 00:50:56,011
I'm sorry.

973
00:50:56,887 --> 00:50:59,723
I had something going on.

974
00:51:03,978 --> 00:51:05,271
Thank you.

975
00:51:08,816 --> 00:51:10,818
- [sighs softly]
- [Mr. Choi] Mmm.

976
00:51:11,485 --> 00:51:13,862
What happened with the case?

977
00:51:14,863 --> 00:51:16,115
We identified a suspect.

978
00:51:17,491 --> 00:51:20,327
We need to catch the guy
who killed Younghwan.

979
00:51:23,247 --> 00:51:25,624
What was it like in jail?

980
00:51:26,292 --> 00:51:28,334
[sighs heavily] It was the worst.

981
00:51:28,335 --> 00:51:30,878
People were throwing up
and snoring next to me.

982
00:51:30,879 --> 00:51:32,839
Crime really doesn't pay.

983
00:51:32,840 --> 00:51:34,425
Wait, I didn't even commit one.

984
00:51:37,261 --> 00:51:38,887
You've been through a lot.

985
00:51:40,472 --> 00:51:42,057
You're worried about me right now?

986
00:51:43,309 --> 00:51:44,976
I heard they're voting you out.

987
00:51:44,977 --> 00:51:46,060
[♪ melancholy music playing]

988
00:51:46,061 --> 00:51:47,520
Ah... [sighs]

989
00:51:47,521 --> 00:51:48,522
You heard?

990
00:51:49,440 --> 00:51:50,940
What's the reason?

991
00:51:50,941 --> 00:51:51,942
Well...

992
00:51:52,943 --> 00:51:53,944
For various reasons.

993
00:51:55,654 --> 00:51:57,031
It was my uncle, wasn't it?

994
00:51:59,658 --> 00:52:01,200
Unbelievable.

995
00:52:01,201 --> 00:52:03,369
He always tries to worm his way in.

996
00:52:03,370 --> 00:52:04,913
No, you're wrong.

997
00:52:05,831 --> 00:52:07,624
It's just time.

998
00:52:07,625 --> 00:52:09,917
So what, you'll go travel the world?

999
00:52:09,918 --> 00:52:12,170
You'll shake it all off
and forget all about me?

1000
00:52:12,171 --> 00:52:13,671
[chuckles softly]

1001
00:52:13,672 --> 00:52:16,425
I have to go. It's my dream.

1002
00:52:19,845 --> 00:52:20,928
[sighs softly]

1003
00:52:20,929 --> 00:52:21,930
[♪ music fades]

1004
00:52:24,266 --> 00:52:27,352
[Mingyun] We will now vote
on the motion to remove the CEO.

1005
00:52:27,353 --> 00:52:30,146
All those in favor, raise your hand.

1006
00:52:30,147 --> 00:52:32,149
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

1007
00:52:35,110 --> 00:52:36,277
[sighs softly]

1008
00:52:36,278 --> 00:52:40,407
With this, the motion to remove the CEO,
Mr. Choi Jeonghun, has passed.

1009
00:52:42,409 --> 00:52:43,494
Chairman Choi.

1010
00:52:44,703 --> 00:52:46,664
Thank you for all your hard work.

1011
00:52:48,415 --> 00:52:50,918
Everyone, let's get up and go.

1012
00:52:56,131 --> 00:52:57,340
[♪ music fades]

1013
00:52:57,341 --> 00:53:00,844
It's been a while since I came in,
and there was an important meeting.

1014
00:53:01,512 --> 00:53:03,222
Please, everyone, have a seat.

1015
00:53:05,224 --> 00:53:07,141
- Mr. Kuk.
- [Mingyun] Yes?

1016
00:53:07,142 --> 00:53:08,477
What motion was passed?

1017
00:53:09,186 --> 00:53:11,896
Uh, the motion to remove the CEO.

1018
00:53:11,897 --> 00:53:13,564
- Really?
- [Mingyun] Yes.

1019
00:53:13,565 --> 00:53:14,733
What was the reason?

1020
00:53:15,609 --> 00:53:17,319
He's not in the best of health.

1021
00:53:18,112 --> 00:53:20,613
The surgery went well,
and he's recovering just fine.

1022
00:53:20,614 --> 00:53:21,698
What else?

1023
00:53:21,699 --> 00:53:24,242
Uh, the unauthorized
high-altitude UAV use.

1024
00:53:24,243 --> 00:53:25,576
That was my request.

1025
00:53:25,577 --> 00:53:27,203
[♪ tense, ticking music playing]

1026
00:53:27,204 --> 00:53:28,287
Anything else?

1027
00:53:28,288 --> 00:53:29,289
Uh...

1028
00:53:30,916 --> 00:53:33,042
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

1029
00:53:33,043 --> 00:53:35,169
It seems after my arrest,

1030
00:53:35,170 --> 00:53:37,798
you were all used by someone
who wants to be the CEO.

1031
00:53:39,883 --> 00:53:42,261
How can I possibly trust this board?

1032
00:53:43,512 --> 00:53:45,264
This isn't your place to interfere.

1033
00:53:48,434 --> 00:53:51,437
As Hansu Group's largest shareholder
and non-executive director,

1034
00:53:52,938 --> 00:53:55,524
I propose a motion to reappoint
Mr. Choi Jeonghun as CEO.

1035
00:53:56,942 --> 00:53:58,985
- Let's vote right away.
- What are you doing?

1036
00:53:58,986 --> 00:54:00,445
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1037
00:54:00,446 --> 00:54:02,029
You think this is a joke?

1038
00:54:02,030 --> 00:54:03,490
All in favor,

1039
00:54:04,199 --> 00:54:05,200
raise your hand.

1040
00:54:13,167 --> 00:54:15,334
It looks like the matter has been settled.

1041
00:54:15,335 --> 00:54:17,129
You should all go. You must be busy.

1042
00:54:28,807 --> 00:54:31,518
They say you get less greedy with age.

1043
00:54:32,394 --> 00:54:34,146
You should really let go now.

1044
00:54:34,897 --> 00:54:37,899
Ah, then again, I do understand.

1045
00:54:37,900 --> 00:54:41,320
Your younger brother always outshone you.
No wonder you're bitter.

1046
00:54:42,196 --> 00:54:43,280
But you should know,

1047
00:54:45,866 --> 00:54:47,743
you're no match for me either, Uncle.

1048
00:54:59,421 --> 00:55:01,381
[♪ electric guitar chord swells]

1049
00:55:04,259 --> 00:55:05,343
[♪ music fades]

1050
00:55:05,344 --> 00:55:06,512
Why did you do that?

1051
00:55:07,262 --> 00:55:10,390
There's no one better suited
to be CEO of Hansu Group than you.

1052
00:55:12,267 --> 00:55:15,436
And I refuse to let you
be pushed out like this because of me.

1053
00:55:15,437 --> 00:55:17,063
[♪ gentle, poignant music playing]

1054
00:55:17,064 --> 00:55:19,941
My uncle's a mean person.

1055
00:55:19,942 --> 00:55:22,235
It'd be bad news
if someone like him became CEO.

1056
00:55:22,236 --> 00:55:23,653
[chuckles]

1057
00:55:23,654 --> 00:55:26,698
I'll personally send you
on that trip myself.

1058
00:55:27,491 --> 00:55:28,492
But until then,

1059
00:55:29,701 --> 00:55:31,203
please look after the company.

1060
00:55:37,459 --> 00:55:39,545
Oh no, I'm late. I'd better go.

1061
00:55:45,592 --> 00:55:47,010
- [sighs heavily]
- [♪ music fades]

1062
00:55:47,594 --> 00:55:48,845
[line ringing]

1063
00:55:53,100 --> 00:55:55,518
- Where is Jin Isoo?
- He won't answer his phone.

1064
00:55:55,519 --> 00:55:57,270
[automated voice]
<i>The number you have dialed...</i>

1065
00:55:57,271 --> 00:55:59,397
- [in English] I'm back.
- Bro.

1066
00:55:59,398 --> 00:56:01,148
What are you wearing?

1067
00:56:01,149 --> 00:56:02,817
[in Korean] I had to stop by somewhere.

1068
00:56:02,818 --> 00:56:04,528
- Are you a trot singer?
- Close enough.

1069
00:56:05,279 --> 00:56:08,115
Cho Pilgu is inside his house.
There on the second floor.

1070
00:56:08,949 --> 00:56:11,742
Detective Park and I will go up.
You stay out of sight.

1071
00:56:11,743 --> 00:56:13,953
Okay, fine. I'll hide near the entrance.

1072
00:56:13,954 --> 00:56:15,454
- Me too.
- [Isoo] Okay.

1073
00:56:15,455 --> 00:56:18,082
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

1074
00:56:18,083 --> 00:56:20,459
Cho Pilgu is dangerous.
We have to be careful.

1075
00:56:20,460 --> 00:56:22,087
- Got it.
- Got it.

1076
00:56:25,591 --> 00:56:27,217
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1077
00:56:39,896 --> 00:56:41,064
[doorbell chiming]

1078
00:56:45,277 --> 00:56:46,569
[Junyoung] I'm from the post office.

1079
00:56:46,570 --> 00:56:48,030
[Pilgu] What do you want?

1080
00:56:49,823 --> 00:56:52,325
Am I speaking to Mr. Cho Pilgu?

1081
00:56:52,326 --> 00:56:55,829
I have a court document
that has to be delivered to you in person.

1082
00:56:58,582 --> 00:57:00,082
[♪ music resumes tempo]

1083
00:57:00,083 --> 00:57:01,418
Could you sign right here?

1084
00:57:08,759 --> 00:57:09,967
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1085
00:57:09,968 --> 00:57:11,428
[Junyoung and Kyungjin grunting]

1086
00:57:13,013 --> 00:57:14,181
[Junyoung grunts, groans]

1087
00:57:14,848 --> 00:57:15,849
Cho Pilgu.

1088
00:57:18,310 --> 00:57:19,519
- [Pilgu grunts]
- [shattering]

1089
00:57:19,936 --> 00:57:21,480
[Pilgu grunts, exhales heavily]

1090
00:57:24,858 --> 00:57:26,276
- Hey, Cho Pilgu.
- [glass shard scrapes]

1091
00:57:27,819 --> 00:57:28,904
- [Pilgu grunts]
- [fabric rips]

1092
00:57:29,905 --> 00:57:31,823
You asshole. This is expensive.

1093
00:57:32,407 --> 00:57:34,076
[both panting]

1094
00:57:34,785 --> 00:57:36,118
- [Junyoung grunts]
- [Kyungjin swears softly]

1095
00:57:36,119 --> 00:57:37,371
[Hyera panting]

1096
00:57:42,542 --> 00:57:43,710
[cycle clatters]

1097
00:57:49,633 --> 00:57:50,758
- [grunts]
- [shattering]

1098
00:57:50,759 --> 00:57:51,927
[Isoo groans]

1099
00:57:56,973 --> 00:57:58,516
[panting]

1100
00:57:58,517 --> 00:57:59,810
[♪ music resumes tempo]

1101
00:58:01,812 --> 00:58:03,187
[grunts, panting]

1102
00:58:03,188 --> 00:58:04,815
[♪ gripping, foreboding music continues]

1103
00:58:06,650 --> 00:58:08,110
[exhales, panting]

1104
00:58:14,491 --> 00:58:16,034
[continues panting] Oh, oh...

1105
00:58:18,787 --> 00:58:20,205
[Isoo continues panting]

1106
00:58:23,375 --> 00:58:25,042
Kid, go inside.

1107
00:58:25,043 --> 00:58:26,420
Go inside!

1108
00:58:28,797 --> 00:58:29,881
[exhales anxiously]

1109
00:58:31,967 --> 00:58:33,259
Your heart's pounding.

1110
00:58:33,260 --> 00:58:34,468
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1111
00:58:34,469 --> 00:58:36,138
[kid breathing shakily]

1112
00:58:37,347 --> 00:58:38,431
Drop the knife.

1113
00:58:38,432 --> 00:58:39,599
[♪ music swells]

1114
00:58:51,236 --> 00:58:52,361
[♪ music fades]

1115
00:58:52,362 --> 00:58:53,446
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 11

1116
00:58:53,447 --> 00:58:54,864
THE CHASE COMES TO A HEAD

1117
00:58:54,865 --> 00:58:56,450
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

1118
00:59:19,389 --> 00:59:22,851
Special Cast. Min Kyoungah

1119
00:59:29,900 --> 00:59:31,358
Why did you kill Younghwan?

1120
00:59:31,359 --> 00:59:32,860
[Kyungjin] <i>Cho Pilgu collapsed!</i>

1121
00:59:32,861 --> 00:59:34,445
[Isoo] <i>But I can't see the bigger picture.</i>

1122
00:59:34,446 --> 00:59:36,238
[Junyoung] <i>Forensics didn't find anything.</i>

1123
00:59:36,239 --> 00:59:37,865
You think you're perfect, don't you?

1124
00:59:37,866 --> 00:59:40,744
I'm working on a new piece.
Would you like to see?

1125
00:59:41,495 --> 00:59:43,329
Are you going to trust someone like her?

1126
00:59:43,330 --> 00:59:44,497
You shut your mouth.

1127
00:59:44,498 --> 00:59:46,291
You have no manners.
You should be careful.

1128
00:59:47,125 --> 00:59:49,752
I think we'll have to kill him.

1129
00:59:49,753 --> 00:59:51,420
<i>Find someone.</i>

1130
00:59:51,421 --> 00:59:52,671
I'm a lawyer.

1131
00:59:52,672 --> 00:59:54,673
[Seongwon] <i>Make him cause an accident.</i>

1132
00:59:54,674 --> 00:59:55,925
It's going to be so much fun.

1133
00:59:55,926 --> 00:59:57,259
Where's Detective Joo?

1134
00:59:57,260 --> 00:59:58,678
How did we get a body delivered?

1135
00:59:59,554 --> 01:00:01,056
[gasps, sobbing]

1136
01:00:02,724 --> 01:00:03,934
[♪ music fades]

1137
01:00:06,645 --> 01:00:07,646
[cell phone vibrating]

1138
01:00:09,439 --> 01:00:10,857
[♪ suspenseful, ominous music playing]

1139
01:00:19,199 --> 01:00:20,951
[cell phone continues vibrating]

1140
01:00:27,123 --> 01:00:28,208
[Pilgu] Mr. Lawyer.

1141
01:00:29,084 --> 01:00:30,794
I've been caught.

1142
01:00:32,045 --> 01:00:33,213
[sighs softly]

1143
01:00:35,924 --> 01:00:37,634
[whispering] You'd better hurry.

1144
01:00:47,561 --> 01:00:49,563
Translated by Hyesoo Lee
